S647 triangular fixed controls and Hamiltonian paths
====================================================

Core identities
---------------
Tournament arc count: A_m = C(m,2)
Fixed Hamiltonian path spine: m-1 forced arcs
Off-path deformation fiber: C(m,2)-(m-1)=C(m-1,2) free arcs
Fixed-path fiber size: 2^C(m-1,2)

Perfect triangular tournament controls
--------------------------------------
  p  m=2^p  arcs=C(m,2)  spine=m-1  offpath=C(m-1,2)  shell=2m-1  status
  1  2      1            1          0                  3          control-only
  2  4      6            3          3                  7          perfect
  3  8      28           7          21                 15         perfect
  4  16     120          15         105                31         control-only
  5  32     496          31         465                63         perfect
  6  64     2016         63         1953               127        control-only
  7  128    8128         127        8001               255        perfect
  8  256    32640        255        32385              511        control-only

The exact perfect controls occur when 2^p-1 is Mersenne prime.
At m=8, the perfect scalar splits as 28 = 7 + 21.
Those are dimensions of a path section and its deformation fiber,
not Hamiltonian-path counts.

Fixed-base-path deformation spectra
-----------------------------------
Rows n=3..7 are enumerated over the 2^C(n-1,2) fixed-path fiber.
Row n=8 is reconstructed from the full labelled n=8 H-spectrum by
fixed_count_h = h * labelled_count_h / 8! .

  n  free_bits  fiber_size  distinct_H  H_range    mean_H      mode       gaps_low
  3  1          2           2           [1,3]     2.0000  3:1       []
  4  3          8           3           [1,5]     4.0000  5:5       []
  5  6          64          7           [1,15]     9.8750  9:18      [7]
  6  10         1024        19          [1,45]    29.0000  37:185     [7, 21, 35, 39]
  7  15         32768       77          [1,189]    99.2188  109:1526    [7, 21, 63]
  8  21         2097152     320         [1,661]   388.6875  523:19874   [7, 21]

